interface — Defines a structural contract of fields, methods, and associated types.

Syntax:
  interface Named {
    type Key = string
    id: Self.Key
    name: string
    function label(self) -> string
    function display(self) -> string {
      return self.name
    }
  }
  
  class Dog {
    id: string
    name: string
    implements Named {
      function label(self) -> string {
        return self.name
      }
    }
  }

Interface fields use `name: Type` syntax. Interfaces can declare associated types with `type Name`, optionally with `extends Bound` and/or `= Default`; use `Self.Name` inside the interface body to refer to the implementing type's binding. A method without a body is required; a method with a body is a default method that implementors inherit unless they override it. Interfaces compose with `requires`, not `extends`.
